                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_16\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit removes try-with-resources wrapping around two ResultSet variables in\nSimpleJDBCRecordStore.java:\n1. In streamAllWithData(): `try (final ResultSet res = stm.executeQuery()) { return allWithDataStream(columns, res); }`\n   is changed back to `final ResultSet res = stm.executeQuery(); return allWithDataStream(columns, res);`\n   with the added comment \"this result-set can't be try-with-resource because it is required to stay open\".\n2. In getValues(tableName, column, condColumn, condValue): the same pattern is reverted for\n   `valuesStream(res)`, with the comment \"can't use try-with-resource here, because result-set is required\n   to stay open\".\n\nBoth allWithDataStream() and valuesStream() return lazily-evaluated Stream objects backed by a\nSpliterator that reads from the ResultSet on each call to tryAdvance(). If the ResultSet is closed\nas soon as the try-with-resources block exits (which happens immediately, since the stream is only\nreturned, not yet consumed), any later attempt to iterate the stream throws \"ResultSet closed\" /\nSQLException, because the JDBC ResultSet resource was released before its data was actually consumed.\n\nSearching the candidates, this exact defective pattern (wrapping `stm.executeQuery()` / `stmt.executeQuery()`\nin a try-with-resources immediately before returning a lazy stream built from allWithDataStream/valuesStream)\ndoes not exist prior to candidate_16. It is candidate_16 that:\n- Refactors the previously inline Spliterator-based stream construction in streamAllWithData() and\n  getValues(...) into the new private helper methods allWithDataStream(...) and valuesStream(...).\n- At the same time, wraps the ResultSet acquisition in `try (final ResultSet res = stm.executeQuery()) { ... }`\n  before calling these new helpers, closing the ResultSet prematurely.\n\nThis is a clean, direct match: the fix commit's diff is the near-exact inverse of the change introduced\nin candidate_16 (same call sites, same helper method names, same try-with-resources pattern being removed).\nNo earlier candidate contains references to allWithDataStream or valuesStream at all, confirming these\ncall sites (and the associated bug) did not exist before candidate_16.\n\nThe fix commit also addresses a resource leak of a PreparedStatement (`PreparedStatement stmt;` declared\nand never closed in insertNewRecord), but that leak pattern already existed in earlier candidates\n(e.g. candidate_09, candidate_13, candidate_15) prior to candidate_16, so it is a separate, older issue\nnot introduced by the selected commit. The primary bug described by the fix - premature closing of a\nResultSet needed to back a lazily-consumed Stream - was introduced in candidate_16.\n"
                }
